The Security Council,

Gravely concerned at the deteriorating humanitarian situation in and around Ukraine, with reports of civilian casualties, including children, and rapidly increasing numbers of internally displaced persons and refugees,

Reiterating the call of the Secretary-General to return to the path of dialogue and negotiations,

Reaffirming the obligation of all States under Article 2 of the Charter of the United Nations to refrain from the threat or use of force against the territorial integrity or political independence of any State, and to settle their international disputes by peaceful means,

Reaffirming its commitment to the sovereignty, independence, unity and territorial integrity of Ukraine,

Reiterating the primary responsibility of States to protect civilians on their respective territories,

Expressing deep concern at all violations of international humanitarian law and violations and abuses of human rights,

Underlining the urgent need to protect civilians and civilian objects, and demanding full respect by all parties for international humanitarian law, including the Geneva Conventions of 1949 and their Additional Protocols,

Stressing that humanitarian assistance must be delivered in accordance with the United Nations guiding principles of humanitarian emergency assistance, including humanity, neutrality, impartiality and independence,

1. Demands that civilians, including humanitarian personnel and persons in vulnerable situations, notably women and children, be fully protected;

2. Demands full respect by all parties for international humanitarian law, and calls on all parties to respect civilian infrastructure and refrain from attacking, destroying, removing or rendering useless objects indispensable to the survival of the civilian population;

3. Calls for a negotiated ceasefire to ensure the rapid, safe, voluntary and unhindered evacuation of all civilians, and underlines the need for the parties concerned to agree on humanitarian pauses to this end;

4. Demands that all parties allow and facilitate the rapid, safe and unhindered access of humanitarian assistance to all those in need, and ensure the safety and security of humanitarian and medical personnel;

5. Strongly condemns all attacks against civilians and civilian infrastructure, as well as any indiscriminate shelling of residential areas;

6. Demands that all parties refrain from establishing military positions in densely populated areas and desist from placing military equipment and personnel in the vicinity of civilian objects, including schools and hospitals, and strictly prohibits the use of civilians as human shields;

7. Urges all parties to facilitate the safe and unhindered departure of all people fleeing the conflict, including foreign nationals, without discrimination, through corridors and to destinations of their own choosing;

8. Encourages Member States to fully fund the United Nations Flash Appeal for Ukraine and the Regional Refugee Response Plan, and to provide comprehensive humanitarian aid to the affected populations;

9. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

